            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="0786" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3642</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gary</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 13, 1921.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 402</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s cable of November 24/6 p.m.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d831-f1"/> sent
                    to Ohristiania, forwarded to us for action, in which the Department states that
                    it would welcome an expression from Dr. Nansen as to the desirability of his
                    continued efforts to secure further releases of Americans now held in
                    Russia.</p>
                <p>I immediately acquainted Dr. Nansen who is in Geneva with the substance of the
                    Department’s telegram and I am this morning in receipt of a reply from him, a
                    copy in translation of which I am enclosing herewith.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hampson Gary</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d831-a1.xml" xpointer="d831-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
